<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Project xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/developer/msbuild/2003">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <XRayVersionMajor>0</XRayVersionMajor>
    <XRayVersionMinor>1</XRayVersionMinor>
    <XRayVersionPatch>1</XRayVersionPatch>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- THE CONFIGURATION THE BINARY WAS BUILT AS, carried into its VERSIONINFO.
       The suites load the tracer from build\addin\, a path that says nothing
       about which configuration put it there, and Debug and Release compile the
       SAME version number from the properties above - so without this a Debug
       XLL can be tested and neither the file nor the result can tell.

       Carried as a NUMBER, never the configuration's name: a define whose value
       is a quoted string does not survive rc.exe's command line, and the
       failure there is silent and total (XRayXL.rc explains at length). The
       resource turns the number back into text.

       Anything that is not exactly Debug or Release yields 2, and the resource
       then reads UNKNOWN rather than quietly claiming Release. This is
       evaluated where $(Configuration) is already established - see the import
       site in XRayXL.vcxproj. -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <XRayBuildConfig>$(Configuration)</XRayBuildConfig>
    <XRayBuildDebugFlag Condition="'$(XRayBuildConfig)'=='Debug'">1</XRayBuildDebugFlag>
    <XRayBuildDebugFlag Condition="'$(XRayBuildConfig)'=='Release'">0</XRayBuildDebugFlag>
    <XRayBuildDebugFlag Condition="'$(XRayBuildDebugFlag)'==''">2</XRayBuildDebugFlag>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
